    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# 🏥 AnamnezAI — AI-Powered Medical Pre-Triage System\\n## Gemma 4 via Ollama | Gemma 4 Good Hackathon 2026\\n\\n[![Gemma 4](https://img.shields.io/badge/Powered%20by-Gemma%204-4285F4)](https://ollama.com/library/gemma4)\\n[![Ollama](https://img.shields.io/badge/Runtime-Ollama%20Local-black)](https://ollama.com)\\n[![License: CC-BY 4.0](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-CC--BY%204.0-green)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)\\n[![Hackathon](https://img.shields.io/badge/Gemma%204%20Good%20Hackathon-Health%20%26%20Sciences-blue)](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/gemma-4-good-hackathon)\\n\\n> **AnamnezAI** automates hospital pre-triage using Gemma 4, running fully locally via Ollama.  \\n> Patients complete a 5-turn AI interview. Doctors receive a structured clinical report with MTS triage priority.  \\n> **Zero cloud API. Zero patient data leaves the device.**\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 📋 Section 1: The Problem — Healthcare Overload\\n\\n### Crisis: Emergency Departments at Breaking Point\\n\\nTurkey's emergency departments face **chronic overload**:\\n\\n| Statistic | Value |\\n|-----------|-------|\\n| Annual emergency visits (Turkey) | **117 million+** (2023, Ministry of Health) |\\n| Time spent on patient intake per visit | **8–15 minutes** (manual anamnesis) |\\n| Patients without pre-triage documentation | **~60%** |\\n| Unnecessary emergency visits (primary-care issues) | **~40%** |\\n\\n### The Root Cause\\nDoctors waste critical time collecting basic history data that patients could provide in advance.  \\nThere is no AI-powered intake layer between the patient and the physician.\\n\\n### AnamnezAI's Solution\\n- Patient completes a **5-turn AI interview** (Gemma 4)\\n- System applies **Manchester Triage System (MTS)** criteria automatically\\n- Doctor receives a **structured clinical report** — red flags highlighted\\n- **No patient data ever leaves the device** (Ollama local inference)\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 🏗️ Section 2: System Architecture\\n\\n```\\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│                         USER LAYER                              │\\n│  ┌──────────┐  ┌───────────┐  ┌───────────────┐  ┌──────────┐  │\\n│  │   Web    │  │   Kiosk   │  │    Doctor     │  │  Admin   │  │\\n│  │ (Patient)│  │  TR / EN  │  │  SSE Queue    │  │Analytics │  │\\n│  │ PWA+TTS  │  │ QR+touch  │  │  Override     │  │ Chart.js │  │\\n│  └────┬─────┘  └─────┬─────┘  └───────┬───────┘  └────┬─────┘  │\\n│       └──────────────┴────────────────┴───────────────┘        │\\n└────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘\\n                             │ HTTP / SSE\\n┌────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│                   FastAPI Backend v5.0                          │\\n│   JWT Auth │ Rate Limit (200/min) │ Audit Log │ SSE │ FHIR R4  │\\n└──────────┬───────────────┬──────────────────┬───────────────────┘\\n           │               │                  │\\n┌──────────▼────┐  ┌───────▼──────────┐  ┌───▼──────────────────┐\\n│    Ollama     │  │    ChromaDB      │  │       SQLite         │\\n│  gemma4:e4b   │  │  ~90 chunks      │  │  sessions/users      │\\n│  medgemma:4b  │  │  all-MiniLM-L6   │  │  audit_log           │\\n│  (optional)   │  │  MTS / ICD-10    │  │                      │\\n└───────────────┘  └──────────────────┘  └──────────────────────┘\\n\\n⚡ All models run LOCALLY via Ollama — Zero API cost\\n⚡ Patient data never leaves the device — KVKK/GDPR compliant\\n```\\n\\n### Key Technical Decisions\\n| Decision | Rationale |\\n|----------|-----------|\\n| **Gemma 4 (gemma4:e4b)** | Multilingual, fits consumer hardware, thinking mode |\\n| **Ollama runtime** | Local inference, no cloud dependency, Docker-friendly |\\n| **ChromaDB RAG** | ~90 medical guideline chunks enrich every triage prompt |\\n| **SSE Streaming** | Real-time clinical summary appears token-by-token for doctors |\\n| **FHIR R4** | Interoperability with hospital HIS systems |\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## ⚙️ Section 3: Setup & Gemma 4 Connection Test\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# Install required packages\\n# Run this cell on Kaggle or locally\\nimport subprocess, sys\\n\\npackages = [\\\"httpx\\\", \\\"pydantic\\\"]\\nfor pkg in packages:\\n    subprocess.run([sys.executable, \\\"-m\\\", \\\"pip\\\", \\\"install\\\", \\\"-q\\\", pkg], check=False)\\n\\nprint(\\\"✅ Packages ready\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"import json\\nimport os\\nimport time\\nimport httpx\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nfrom typing import Optional\\n\\n# ─── Configuration ───\\nOLLAMA_BASE_URL = os.getenv(\\\"OLLAMA_BASE_URL\\\", \\\"http://localhost:11434\\\")\\nGEMMA_MODEL = os.getenv(\\\"GEMMA_MODEL\\\", \\\"gemma4:e4b\\\")\\nANAMNEZAI_URL = os.getenv(\\\"ANAMNEZAI_URL\\\", \\\"http://localhost:8000\\\")\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Ollama URL : {OLLAMA_BASE_URL}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Model      : {GEMMA_MODEL}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Backend URL: {ANAMNEZAI_URL}\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"def test_gemma4_connection() -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test that Gemma 4 is available via Ollama.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        with httpx.Client(timeout=10.0) as client:\\n            r = client.get(f\\\"{OLLAMA_BASE_URL}/api/tags\\\")\\n            models = [m[\\\"name\\\"] for m in r.json().get(\\\"models\\\", [])]\\n            gemma4_found = any(\\\"gemma4\\\" in m for m in models)\\n            return {\\n                \\\"ollama_running\\\": True,\\n                \\\"gemma4_available\\\": gemma4_found,\\n                \\\"loaded_models\\\": models,\\n            }\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        return {\\\"ollama_running\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": str(e), \\\"gemma4_available\\\": False}\\n\\nresult = test_gemma4_connection()\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n=== Gemma 4 Connection Test ===\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  Ollama running  : {result['ollama_running']}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  Gemma 4 loaded  : {result.get('gemma4_available', False)}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  All models      : {result.get('loaded_models', [])}\\\")\\nif result.get(\\\"gemma4_available\\\"):\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n✅ Gemma 4 is ready — proceeding with demo\\\")\\nelse:\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n⚠️  Run: ollama pull gemma4:e4b && ollama serve\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 🧠 Section 4: AnamnezAI Core Engine (Gemma 4)\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# ─── MTS-based System Prompts ───\\n\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT_EN = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are AnamnezAI — an experienced, empathetic medical pre-triage assistant.\\nPowered by Gemma 4, running 100% locally via Ollama.\\nTASK: Ask clinically relevant, contextual questions to understand the patient's symptoms.\\nRULES:\\n- Ask ONLY ONE question at a time (max 2 sentences).\\n- Build questions from ALL previous answers (contextual interview).\\n- EMERGENCY signs (chest pain, breathing difficulty, loss of consciousness, stroke): explore FIRST.\\n- Apply MTS criteria: radiation, severity (1-10), duration, triggers, associated symptoms.\\n- Empathetic, calming tone. End with a question mark.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nTRIAGE_SYSTEM_EN = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a clinical triage expert trained on MTS (Manchester Triage System) and CTAS standards.\\nPowered by Gemma 4. Analyze the patient interview history.\\nOUTPUT: Return ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\n{\\n  \\\"triage_level\\\": \\\"RED or YELLOW or GREEN\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence_score\\\": 0-100,\\n  \\\"chief_complaint\\\": \\\"One clear sentence\\\",\\n  \\\"symptoms_summary\\\": \\\"2-3 sentences\\\",\\n  \\\"possible_conditions\\\": [\\\"Most likely\\\", \\\"Second\\\", \\\"Third\\\"],\\n  \\\"recommended_action\\\": \\\"One sentence\\\",\\n  \\\"clinical_notes\\\": \\\"Critical observations for physician, 2-3 sentences\\\",\\n  \\\"urgency_flags\\\": [\\\"Flags if any\\\"],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"Clinical finding 1\\\", \\\"Finding 2\\\", \\\"Finding 3\\\"],\\n  \\\"guideline_sources\\\": [\\\"MTS Discriminator used\\\", \\\"CTAS level\\\"]\\n}\\nRED = Life-threatening / immediate (AMI, stroke, anaphylaxis, respiratory failure, GCS<8)\\nYELLOW = Urgent, seen within 30min-2hrs (high fever, moderate pain, hypertensive urgency)\\nGREEN = Routine outpatient (mild symptoms, chronic follow-up, URTI)\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nprint(\\\"✅ MTS system prompts loaded\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"class AnamnezAIEngine:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Minimal AnamnezAI engine for notebook demonstration.\\n    \\n    Uses Gemma 4 via Ollama for:\\n    1. Dynamic interview question generation\\n    2. MTS triage classification\\n    3. Structured clinical report generation\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, model: str = GEMMA_MODEL, base_url: str = OLLAMA_BASE_URL):\\n        self.model = model\\n        self.base_url = base_url\\n        self._call_times: list[float] = []\\n\\n    def _ask(self, prompt: str, system: str = \\\"\\\", timeout: float = 120.0) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Send prompt to Gemma 4 via Ollama /api/chat.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        t0 = time.time()\\n        messages = []\\n        if system:\\n            messages.append({\\\"role\\\": \\\"system\\\", \\\"content\\\": system})\\n        messages.append({\\\"role\\\": \\\"user\\\", \\\"content\\\": prompt})\\n        with httpx.Client(timeout=timeout) as client:\\n            resp = client.post(\\n                f\\\"{self.base_url}/api/chat\\\",\\n                json={\\n                    \\\"model\\\": self.model,\\n                    \\\"messages\\\": messages,\\n                    \\\"stream\\\": False,\\n                    \\\"think\\\": False,\\n                    \\\"options\\\": {\\\"temperature\\\": 0.25, \\\"top_p\\\": 0.85, \\\"num_predict\\\": 512},\\n                },\\n            )\\n            resp.raise_for_status()\\n        elapsed = time.time() - t0\\n        self._call_times.append(elapsed)\\n        return resp.json()[\\\"message\\\"][\\\"content\\\"].strip()\\n\\n    def generate_question(self, patient_name: str, age: int, gender: str,\\n                          qa_history: list[dict], step: int, total: int) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate next contextual interview question using Gemma 4.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        history_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(\\n            f\\\"Q{i+1}: {qa['q']}\\\\nA: {qa['a']}\\\"\\n            for i, qa in enumerate(qa_history)\\n            if qa.get(\\\"a\\\")\\n        )\\n        if not history_text:\\n            prompt = (\\n                f\\\"Patient: {patient_name}, {age}y, {gender}.\\\\n\\\"\\n                f\\\"First visit. Ask an empathetic opening question to learn their main complaint. Q1/{total}.\\\"\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            prompt = (\\n                f\\\"Patient: {patient_name}, {age}y, {gender}.\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                f\\\"Interview so far:\\\\n{history_text}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                f\\\"Ask the NEXT most critical question. If emergency signs present, explore further. Q{step}/{total}.\\\"\\n            )\\n        return self._ask(prompt, SYSTEM_PROMPT_EN)\\n\\n    def generate_triage(self, patient_name: str, age: int, gender: str,\\n                        qa_history: list[dict]) -> dict:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate MTS triage classification using Gemma 4.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        history_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(\\n            f\\\"Q{i+1}: {qa['q']}\\\\nA: {qa['a']}\\\"\\n            for i, qa in enumerate(qa_history)\\n        )\\n        prompt = (\\n            f\\\"PATIENT: {patient_name}, {age}y, {gender}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            f\\\"INTERVIEW:\\\\n{history_text}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            f\\\"Triage this patient. Return ONLY JSON.\\\"\\n        )\\n        raw = self._ask(prompt, TRIAGE_SYSTEM_EN)\\n        # Parse JSON robustly\\n        try:\\n            start, end = raw.find(\\\"{\\\"), raw.rfind(\\\"}\\\") + 1\\n            return json.loads(raw[start:end])\\n        except Exception:\\n            return {\\\"triage_level\\\": \\\"YELLOW\\\", \\\"confidence_score\\\": 50,\\n                    \\\"chief_complaint\\\": \\\"Parse error\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw[:200]}\\n\\n    def get_performance_stats(self) -> dict:\\n        if not self._call_times:\\n            return {\\\"total_calls\\\": 0}\\n        return {\\n            \\\"total_calls\\\": len(self._call_times),\\n            \\\"avg_latency_s\\\": round(sum(self._call_times) / len(self._call_times), 2),\\n            \\\"min_latency_s\\\": round(min(self._call_times), 2),\\n            \\\"max_latency_s\\\": round(max(self._call_times), 2),\\n            \\\"model\\\": self.model,\\n        }\\n\\n\\nai = AnamnezAIEngine()\\nprint(f\\\"✅ AnamnezAI Engine initialised — model: {GEMMA_MODEL}\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 🎭 Section 5: Simulated Patient Interviews — 3 Clinical Scenarios\\n\\n| # | Patient | Age | Chief Complaint | Expected Triage |\\n|---|---------|-----|-----------------|-----------------|\\n| 1 | John Smith | 58M | Crushing chest pain, left arm radiation | 🔴 RED |\\n| 2 | Maria Lopez | 34F | High fever + headache + neck stiffness | 🟡 YELLOW |\\n| 3 | Tom Baker | 42M | Sore throat + mild cough | 🟢 GREEN |\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"TRIAGE_EMOJI = {\\\"RED\\\": \\\"🔴\\\", \\\"YELLOW\\\": \\\"🟡\\\", \\\"GREEN\\\": \\\"🟢\\\"}\\nTRIAGE_LABEL = {\\\"RED\\\": \\\"IMMEDIATE\\\", \\\"YELLOW\\\": \\\"URGENT\\\", \\\"GREEN\\\": \\\"ROUTINE\\\"}\\nCOLOR_BAR   = {\\\"RED\\\": \\\"█\\\", \\\"YELLOW\\\": \\\"▓\\\", \\\"GREEN\\\": \\\"░\\\"}\\n\\n# Pre-defined interview answers for reproducible demo\\n# In production, the patient types these answers in real-time\\nSCENARIOS = [\\n    {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"John Smith\\\", \\\"age\\\": 58, \\\"gender\\\": \\\"Male\\\",\\n        \\\"answers\\\": [\\n            \\\"I have crushing chest pain since this morning.\\\",\\n            \\\"Yes, it radiates down my left arm. About 8/10 severity.\\\",\\n            \\\"I am sweating a lot and feel nauseous too.\\\",\\n            \\\"No known heart problems but my father had a heart attack.\\\",\\n            \\\"The pain is not going away. I feel short of breath.\\\",\\n        ],\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"Maria Lopez\\\", \\\"age\\\": 34, \\\"gender\\\": \\\"Female\\\",\\n        \\\"answers\\\": [\\n            \\\"I have had a very high fever and severe headache for two days.\\\",\\n            \\\"About 39.8°C my husband took it. The headache is 7/10.\\\",\\n            \\\"My neck feels stiff and I cannot look down comfortably.\\\",\\n            \\\"No recent travel. I am sensitive to light too.\\\",\\n            \\\"I have not taken any medication yet.\\\",\\n        ],\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"Tom Baker\\\", \\\"age\\\": 42, \\\"gender\\\": \\\"Male\\\",\\n        \\\"answers\\\": [\\n            \\\"I have a sore throat and mild cough since yesterday.\\\",\\n            \\\"The pain is about 3/10. No fever that I know of.\\\",\\n            \\\"No difficulty swallowing or breathing.\\\",\\n            \\\"I had a cold a few weeks ago, this feels similar.\\\",\\n            \\\"I take no medications and have no chronic conditions.\\\",\\n        ],\\n    },\\n]\\n\\nprint(\\\"✅ 3 clinical scenarios loaded\\\")\\nprint(\\\"   🔴 Case 1: Chest pain — AMI pattern (expected RED)\\\")\\nprint(\\\"   🟡 Case 2: Fever + neck stiffness (expected YELLOW)\\\")\\nprint(\\\"   🟢 Case 3: Sore throat (expected GREEN)\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"def run_interview(ai_engine: AnamnezAIEngine, scenario: dict, total_steps: int = 5) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Run a full simulated 5-question patient interview using Gemma 4.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    name, age, gender = scenario[\\\"name\\\"], scenario[\\\"age\\\"], scenario[\\\"gender\\\"]\\n    pre_answers = scenario[\\\"answers\\\"]\\n    qa_history: list[dict] = []\\n\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n{'='*64}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  PATIENT: {name}, {age}y, {gender}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"{'='*64}\\\")\\n\\n    for step in range(1, total_steps + 1):\\n        question = ai_engine.generate_question(name, age, gender, qa_history, step, total_steps)\\n        answer   = pre_answers[step - 1] if step <= len(pre_answers) else \\\"(no answer)\\\"\\n        qa_history.append({\\\"q\\\": question, \\\"a\\\": answer})\\n        print(f\\\"\\\\n  Q{step}: {question}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  A{step}: {answer}\\\")\\n\\n    triage = ai_engine.generate_triage(name, age, gender, qa_history)\\n    level  = triage.get(\\\"triage_level\\\", \\\"YELLOW\\\")\\n    conf   = triage.get(\\\"confidence_score\\\", 0)\\n    emoji  = TRIAGE_EMOJI.get(level, \\\"⚪\\\")\\n    label  = TRIAGE_LABEL.get(level, level)\\n    bar_ch = COLOR_BAR.get(level, \\\"░\\\")\\n    bar    = bar_ch * int(conf / 5)\\n\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n  {'─'*60}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  TRIAGE RESULT  {emoji} {level} — {label}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Confidence     [{bar:<20}] {conf}%\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Chief Complaint: {triage.get('chief_complaint', '')}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Likely Conditions: {', '.join(triage.get('possible_conditions', [])[:3])}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Action: {triage.get('recommended_action', '')}\\\")\\n    evidence = triage.get('evidence', [])\\n    if evidence:\\n        print(f\\\"  Evidence: {' | '.join(evidence[:2])}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  {'─'*60}\\\")\\n\\n    return {\\\"patient\\\": scenario, \\\"qa_history\\\": qa_history, \\\"triage\\\": triage}\\n\\n\\n# Run Case 1 — Chest Pain (AMI pattern)\\nresult1 = run_interview(ai, SCENARIOS[0])\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# Run Case 2 — Fever + Neck Stiffness\\nresult2 = run_interview(ai, SCENARIOS[1])\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# Run Case 3 — Sore Throat (GREEN expected)\\nresult3 = run_interview(ai, SCENARIOS[2])\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 📊 Section 6: Doctor Triage Queue Visualisation\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": \"PRIORITY = {\\\"RED\\\": 0, \\\"YELLOW\\\": 1, \\\"GREEN\\\": 2}\\nresults  = [result1, result2, result3]\\n\\n# Sort by triage priority\\nqueue = sorted(results, key=lambda r: PRIORITY.get(r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"triage_level\\\", \\\"GREEN\\\"), 2))\\n\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"=\\\" * 70)\\nprint(\\\"  DOCTOR TRIAGE QUEUE — AnamnezAI Real-Time Dashboard\\\")\\nprint(\\\"=\\\" * 70)\\nprint(f\\\"  {'#':<3} {'PATIENT':<22} {'TRIAGE':<10} {'CONF':>5}   CHIEF COMPLAINT\\\")\\nprint(\\\"  \\\" + \\\"─\\\" * 66)\\n\\nfor i, r in enumerate(queue, 1):\\n    name   = r[\\\"patient\\\"][\\\"name\\\"]\\n    level  = r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"triage_level\\\", \\\"YELLOW\\\")\\n    conf   = r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"confidence_score\\\", 0)\\n    cc     = r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"chief_complaint\\\", \\\"—\\\")[:35]\\n    emoji  = TRIAGE_EMOJI.get(level, \\\"⚪\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  {i:<3} {name:<22} {emoji}{level:<9} {conf:>4}%   {cc}\\\")\\n\\nprint()\\nred_cnt    = sum(1 for r in results if r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"triage_level\\\") == \\\"RED\\\")\\nyellow_cnt = sum(1 for r in results if r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"triage_level\\\") == \\\"YELLOW\\\")\\ngreen_cnt  = sum(1 for r in results if r[\\\"triage\\\"].get(\\\"triage_level\\\") == \\\"GREEN\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  SUMMARY: 🔴 RED={red_cnt}  🟡 YELLOW={yellow_cnt}  🟢 GREEN={green_cnt}  |  Total={len(results)}\\\")\\nprint()\\n\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## ⚡ Section 7: Performance Metrics\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
